    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d734">

                <pb facs="0827" n="633" xml:id="pg633"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.014/6–2045</note>
                <head>No. 734<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gromyko</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20">July 20, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am sending you herewith in
                    accordance with your request expressed at the time of our conversation this
                    morning, a copy of my letter and the letter of former Secretary of State
                    Stettinius on the question of territorial trusteeships. We exchanged these
                    letters while at San Francisco at the time of the United Nations Conference.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gromyko</hi></signed></closer>




